  "releaseNotes": "`PrefixWeightedSequence<T>.Move` moves a node to a new position by taking it out where it stands and reinserting it where it belongs, touching two paths through the sequence where moving a range of one by position touches six.\n`ObservableRangeCollection<T>.MoveRange` moving one element shifts only the elements between its two places, where it shifted everything after each of them, and announces the move with a single-element list rather than a `List<T>`, 72 bytes of event arguments rather than 160.",
